      "content": "that's a pretty big distinction you're making between the two. it sounds like you're suggesting that even with training, there's a different baseline of \"professionalism\" or \"attention to detail\" that comes naturally to the european groups but has to be forced or heavily managed in africa or se asia. \n\nwhen you talk about \"deeper cultural work values\" and \"variable work ethic,\" are you essentially saying that there is a more innate level of temperament or discipline in the european worker that just isn't as present in these other regions? like, is it a question of whether certain populations are fundamentally more suited to high-level, responsible roles?",
      "source": "evaluator"
